      "evidence": "Slide 2 quantifies the pain ('20+ hours/week') and names the ICP (indie SaaS founders), which establishes specificity. However, the cost of inaction is not quantified in dollars or missed revenue, no budget owner is identified, and no urgency trigger is shown. Without a dollar-cost framing and a clear buyer, the problem reads as an inconvenience rather than an urgent, funded pain. The common-mistakes standard requires urgency, a budget owner, and a quantified cost of inaction.",
