      "status": "fail",
      "evidence": "Slide 3 describes the solution as 'Acmecorp wraps GitHub, Linear, Stripe, and Vercel into one CLI.' This is a technical feature description — it names what the product does architecturally, not what outcome the user gets. No before/after workflow, no time-saved metric, and no user result is shown on the solution slide. Sequoia's solution-slide standard and the common-mistakes framework both require focusing on value delivered rather than technical architecture.",
      "notes": "Replace the feature description with an outcome statement: e.g., 'Indie SaaS founders cut integration time from 20 hours/week to under 2 hours — without touching a single API doc.' Then add the technical details (CLI, tool list) as supporting evidence beneath the outcome headline."
